The class `FlowableMapPublisher` is a thin delegating wrapper that merely forwards subscription to the upstream `Publisher` and applies a mapper via `MapSubscriber`. Its behavior and performance are entirely dependent on the upstream source and the mapper function, not on any complex logic within this class itself. Consequently, a dedicated JMH benchmark would not yield meaningful insights about this class in isolation, and any performance measurement should target realistic end‑to‑end reactive pipelines rather than this trivial wrapper. Hence, generating a JMH benchmark is unnecessary.